01:29:00.280 --> 01:29:02.760
How did that apprenticeship with the Bay Area scene

01:29:02.760 --> 01:29:05.700
actually help you prepare for your role in Slayer?

01:29:05.820 --> 01:29:07.520
Because it's quite an aggressive scene, isn't it?

01:29:07.760 --> 01:29:10.680
Yeah, I think that answers the question right there

01:29:10.680 --> 01:29:13.980
because it was actually aggressive and quite competitive.

01:29:14.560 --> 01:29:19.760
There was bands like Violence, Death Angel, Exodus, Forbidden,

01:29:21.860 --> 01:29:24.920
just to name a few of the bands, Heathen.

01:29:25.140 --> 01:29:29.960
And just between all those bands, I think that it forced

01:29:30.000 --> 01:29:34.920
us all to create some quality music and you know actually push ourselves as musicians and you know

01:29:34.920 --> 01:29:40.220
so it was a good uh training ground oh yeah yeah now um for you i know you're a big slayer fan

01:29:40.220 --> 01:29:45.120
before you joined the band but what was the biggest challenge for you personally about joining

01:29:45.120 --> 01:29:51.140
a world-class band like slayer quite honestly i'd have to say um reproducing dave's drum lines

01:29:51.140 --> 01:29:56.150
was the biggest challenge for me um playing the music and understanding the arrangements and

01:29:56.150 --> 01:29:59.530
all that I mean I knew all that stuff it was just trying to

01:30:00.220 --> 01:30:04.370
trying to emulate somebody else's style and, you know, actually do it justice

01:30:04.370 --> 01:30:07.990
as opposed to just going, okay, throwing that out the window and trying to do my own thing.

01:30:08.460 --> 01:30:11.380
But you've definitely done that, I think, to the consensus of opinion,

01:30:11.420 --> 01:30:15.550
but you've also obviously injected some of your own individuality

01:30:16.230 --> 01:30:18.810
into the drum patterns on Divine Intervention as well.

01:30:19.230 --> 01:30:20.610
That was my goal.

01:30:20.770 --> 01:30:26.000
Do the old stuff with honor or whatever you want to call it, you know, authentically,

01:30:26.000 --> 01:30:28.480
and then, you know, on the new stuff, just do whatever I want to do.

01:30:28.940 --> 01:30:29.740
You certainly achieved it.

01:30:30.000 --> 01:30:30.520
So, congratulations.

01:30:31.280 --> 01:30:33.720
I mean, how was it, we talked a little bit about this earlier,

01:30:33.880 --> 01:30:37.720
but for you, how was it to come into a situation with three guys

01:30:37.720 --> 01:30:40.340
that had been working together for over ten years?

01:30:40.580 --> 01:30:42.740
How was it for you to come into that?

01:30:43.700 --> 01:30:47.560
You must have felt very comfortable from the very first minute, I would imagine.

01:30:48.500 --> 01:30:49.760
They made me feel comfortable.

01:30:50.040 --> 01:30:51.940
When I first came in, I didn't know what to expect,

01:30:52.140 --> 01:30:54.560
so it was a little uneasiness, you know,

01:30:54.700 --> 01:30:57.620
because I'm kind of a shy person when I first meet people,

01:30:57.800 --> 01:30:59.980
so I didn't know what to expect.

01:31:00.000 --> 01:31:04.390
respect and these guys like kind of made it easy and as far as like coming into a chemistry of a

01:31:04.390 --> 01:31:09.250
band that's been around for 10 years it was more or less I had to like for my old band that I was in

01:31:09.250 --> 01:31:14.170
I was like more up front you know it was everything more on top of the totem pole if you want to call

01:31:14.170 --> 01:31:18.670
it and then I came into this situation like all the way in the bottom so it was a totally different

01:31:18.670 --> 01:31:22.950
perspective so I had to back off and like just let things take their course in front of me and

01:31:22.950 --> 01:31:27.250
anywhere where I saw a space where I could fill in or enhance something I did instead of trying

01:31:27.250 --> 01:31:28.900
to change something, you know.

01:31:29.340 --> 01:31:29.980
It's a very exciting...

01:31:30.000 --> 01:31:34.000
time for you right now with the european tour and all these great things happening for slayer

01:31:34.000 --> 01:31:39.240
it's great you must think you're in a dream or something uh yeah well thanks very much paul

01:31:39.240 --> 01:31:45.960
for that insight into your role in slayer in 1994 and as we've all realized i think by now after

01:31:45.960 --> 01:31:51.730
listening to divine intervention the band are firing on all four cylinders and they are in fine

01:31:51.730 --> 01:31:56.940
form so we're going to let paul go off now and do his sound check down at the gig at the ulster hall

01:31:56.940 --> 01:31:59.800
and we're going to be following the band down there right now.

